he brainstem in mice with gastritis</article-title><source>Neuroscience</source><year>2007</year><volume>145</volume><fpage>1108</fpage><lpage>19</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17303342</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B11"><mixed-citation publication-type="book"><name><surname>Kirk</surname><given-names>RE</given-names></name><source>Experimental Design: Procedures for Behavioral Sciences: Procedures for the Behavioral Sciences</source><year>1995</year><publisher-name>Pacific Grove, California: Brooks/Cole</publisher-name></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B12"><mixed-citation publication-type="book"><name><surname>Hays</surname><given-names>WL</given-names></name><source>Statistics</source><year>2007</year><publisher-name>Belmont: Wadsworth</publisher-name></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B13"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Munglani</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Hunt</surname><given-names>SP</given-names></name><article-title>Proto-oncogenes: basic concepts and stimulation induced changes in the spinal cord</article-title><source>Prog Brain Res</source><year>1995</year><volume>104</volume><fpage>283</fpage><lpage>98</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8552774</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B14"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Kov&#x000e1;cs</surname><given-names>KJ</given-names></name><article-title>c-Fos as a transcription factor: a stressful (re)view from a functional map</article-title><source>Neurochem Int</source><year>1998</year><volume>33</volume><fpage>287</fpage><lpage>97</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9840219</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B15"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Okayama</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Tsubouchi</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Kato</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Takeuchi</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name